  "2": "The function we must write. It gets the `grid` and returns the area of the biggest island.",
  "3": "A helper that returns how many land cells the island containing this cell has, marking them as visited.",
  "4": "Is this cell outside the grid, or is it water (`0`)?",
  "11": "Then it adds no area.",
  "13": "Mark this land cell as visited by turning it into water, so it is counted only once.",
  "14": "This cell counts as 1.",
  "16": "Add the land reachable through the cell below (the helper calls itself).",
  "17": "Add the land reachable through the cell above.",
  "18": "Add the land reachable through the cell to the right.",
  "19": "Add the land reachable through the cell to the left.",
  "21": "Report the total area found from here.",
  "23": "The biggest area found so far.",
  "24": "Scan every row of the grid…",
  "25": "…and every column in it.",
  "26": "Is this land that has not been visited yet?",
  "27": "Measure its whole island, and keep the bigger of that and the best so far.",
  "29": "Return the biggest area."
 },
